{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/lem-bar-involution-parity-decomposition","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Lemma","doco:Section"],"label":"lem:bar-involution-parity-decomposition","kind":"lemma","title":"Even/odd decomposition under a linear involution","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-bar-involution"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-bar-involution-parity-decomposition"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Mass.evenPart_add_oddPart","text":"bar-involution-parity-decomposition.md","leanSource":"bar-involution-parity-decomposition.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"lem:bar-involution-parity-decomposition\"></a><p><em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma</code> be an <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-linear map of an <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-module <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma^2 = \\mathrm{id}</code>. For <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">x \\in V</code> put</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">\\mathrm{even}(x) = x + \\sigma x, \\qquad \\mathrm{odd}(x) = x - \\sigma x.</code></pre>\n<p><em>Then <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{even}(x) + \\mathrm{odd}(x) = 2x</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma(\\mathrm{even}(x)) = \\mathrm{even}(x)</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma(\\mathrm{odd}(x)) = -\\mathrm{odd}(x)</code>.</em></p>\n<p>The lemma applies in particular to the bar-involution <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\mapsto q^{-1}</code> of <a href=\"#def:bar-involution\">Bar-involution and its <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">P_{\\mathrm{avg}}</code> / <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">P_{\\mathrm{skew}}</code> projections</a>. It holds for every element of every such module, so it says nothing about which element a given observable is the even or odd part of.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/bar-involution-parity-decomposition.md","heading":"Lemma","number":"13.7.60","page":"b/lem-bar-involution-parity-decomposition","qa":{"counts":{"pass":1,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":0,"unknown":0,"stale":1}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.Mass.evenPart_add_oddPart","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/bar-involution-parity-decomposition.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
